# A loaded game opens in Explore mode, and Explore answers every move the human
# makes. A click on the move the record already has is not one: it follows, as
# the Right arrow does. The engine replied to it all the same — and its reply
# went in as the first child, over the game actually played, taking RE with it.
# Reviewing a finished game by clicking its next-move marker rewrote it.
#
# tests/data/finished_9x9.sgf opens with B[fe], which is `click 5 4`.

load_sgf tests/data/finished_9x9.sgf
wait_idle
expect mode explore
navigate_start
wait_idle
expect view_position 0

click 5 4
click 5 4
wait_until view_position >= 1
wait 800
wait_idle
expect view_position 1
expect main_line_moves 37
expect has_result true
expect unsaved_changes false
expect phase paused

# A move the record does not have is still answered — in a copy.
click 0 0
click 0 0
wait_until view_position >= 3
wait_idle
expect view_position 3
expect sgf_file ""
